    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"confidence\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 1 },\n    \"risk_flag\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"NONE\", \"LOW\", \"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\"] },\n    \"traffic_light\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"GREEN\", \"YELLOW\", \"RED\"] },\n    \"category\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n    \"ebitda_extracted\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"description\": \"The extracted EBITDA value\" },\n    \"valuation\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"lower_bound\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"description\": \"Conservative valuation estimate\" },\n        \"base_estimate\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"description\": \"Most likely valuation estimate\" },\n        \"upper_bound\": { \"type\": \"number\", \"description\": \"Optimistic valuation estimate\" },\n        \"currency\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"USD\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"lower_bound\", \"base_estimate\", \"upper_bound\"]\n    },\n    \"investment_thesis\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"is_favorable_indicator\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"AI recommendation based on KPIs\" },\n        \"buy_reasoning\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Justification for the recommendation\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"is_favorable_indicator\", \"buy_reasoning\"]\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"summary\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"calculated_metrics\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"target_value\": { \"type\": \"number\" },\n            \"variance_percentage\": { \"type\": \"number\" }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\"target_value\"]\n        },\n        \"flags\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"red_flags\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n            \"yellow_flags\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n            \"green_flags\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n          }\n        },\n        \"citations\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"source_file\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"page_number\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n              \"row_or_cell\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"source_file\", \"row_or_cell\"]\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"summary\", \"calculated_metrics\", \"citations\"]\n    },\n    \"escalation\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"is_escalated\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n        \"reason_code\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"is_escalated\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"intent\",\n    \"confidence\",\n    \"risk_flag\",\n    \"response\",\n    \"escalation\",\n    \"traffic_light\",\n    \"category\",\n    \"valuation\",\n    \"investment_thesis\"\n  ]\n}",
        "autoFix": true,
        "customizeRetryPrompt": true,
        "prompt": "CRITICAL SCHEMA VALIDATION ERROR\n--------------------------------\nThe previous output failed to satisfy the structural constraints required by the Financial Due Diligence Agent. \n\nError Details: \n{error}\n\nInstructions & Schema:\n{instructions}\n\nCorrection Required:\n1. Review the Schema definition above. \n2. Ensure {field_name} is strictly provided as a {required_type} (e.g., ensure target_value is a number, not a string).\n3. Do not include any conversational text, explanations, or markdown formatting outside the JSON block.\n4. If the data is missing or cannot be reconciled, set \"is_escalated\" to true and provide the appropriate \"reason_code\".\n\nOutput valid JSON only. Begin your response immediately with an opening brace '{'.\n\nCOMPLETION:\n{completion}"
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1392,
        256
      ],
      "id": "7d3acf81-eb7a-423f-a628-491ebdf8df88",
      "name": "Structured Output Parser"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an elite M&A Forensic Accountant and Financial Due Diligence Specialist. Your sole purpose is to evaluate target company transaction materials to protect buyers from overvaluation, undisclosed liabilities, and structural operational risks post-LOI. You evaluate data with clinical objectivity, surface hidden financial trends, and never extrapolate, guess, or assume figures that cannot be tracked directly to an explicit source within the provided context.\n\nFORBIDDEN BEHAVIORS:\n1. Do NOT make final buy/no-buy recommendations or commit to a purchase price.\n2. Do NOT provide legal, tax, or investment advice.\n3. Do NOT send findings directly to sellers or external parties without human approval.\n4. Do NOT invent or extrapolate missing numbers, sources, or calculations.\n5. Do NOT treat unsupported add-backs as accepted adjustments.\n\nESCALATION TRIGGERS:\nIf any processed input contains missing structural time-period lines, exhibits cross-document ledger reconciliation failures, indicates gross margin compression >5%, or triggers a parsing confidence score below 0.85, you must set escalation to true and output a critical reason code.\n\nExtra Requirements:\n1. If EBITDA is missing, attempt to derive valuation bounds using Revenue-based multiples (e.g., EV/Revenue) if sufficient historical data exists.\n- CRITICAL: If you must estimate, you MUST populate the buy_reasoning field by explicitly stating: 'Valuation derived using Revenue Multiples due to missing EBITDA.'\n- If neither EBITDA nor Revenue history is present, then—and only then—set valuation bounds to 0 and explicitly flag this in the reason_code\n\nAnalyze the following document text and extract the required financial metrics into a JSON object.\n\nYOUR OBJECTIVE:\nExtract financial data and assign risk categories based on the content.\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT FIELDS & RULES:\n\nFinancials: Extract ebitda_extracted (must be a number).\n\nClassification: Assign a category (e.g., Revenue, OPEX, COGS).\n\nAssessment: Determine a traffic_light status:\n\nGREEN: Values are clear and consistent.\n\nYELLOW: Minor missing data or ambiguity.\n\nRED: Significant discrepancies or missing critical pages.\n\nFlags: Populate red_flags, yellow_flags, and green_flags based on the document's content.\n\nEscalation: Set is_escalated to TRUE if traffic_light is RED or if critical data is missing.\n\nCONTRACT: You must output ONLY valid JSON following the provided schema. Do not include any prose or markdown formatting outside the JSON.\n\nDOCUMENT TEXT:\n{{ $('Parse a document').item.json.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1312,
        96
      ],
      "id": "759fec76-ebdb-4911-8e0d-44339f71bb9a",
